[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186083272 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9cdf7c4f-4409-57f0-b1eb-dca5de834f65" "question-522d89ff-41d6-50ec-8d1b-a4ada325fbc8" "question-d66ccea1-6118-5ac8-bad9-91d326fbbfdc" "question-0298a94b-23a5-5b8c-89b1-b11dd1bda638"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083308 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-53e1317a-3ae2-58ac-bb4d-59a740997145" "question-6f220269-fce2-5308-a544-a882143be2b5" "question-dc6b2040-54a4-56f7-9767-230b7779b10f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083309 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ceddea1b-a5cb-5c22-91ab-6571fb7ef388" "question-700fffbb-cd63-5378-9077-32b4c2add6e6" "question-41c4d9f2-fb24-5742-893b-e72bc5478b30" "question-d599b4ec-9437-5cdd-aa0b-91b4481a6586"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083273 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-068e9bc7-6f46-5ac9-a057-d5f4aa9a8aeb" "question-267e0e90-b604-5e86-ad43-795951237ad2"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-9cdf7c4f-4409-57f0-b1eb-dca5de834f65" :question/id #uuid "9cdf7c4f-4409-57f0-b1eb-dca5de834f65" :question/math-academy-id "q-276297" :question/problem "A fair spinner has six sides labeled with the numbers $-2,$ $-1,$ $0,$ $1,$ $2,$ and $3.$ If the spinner is spun, what is the expected value of the outcome?\n\n$\\text{E}[X]=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the outcome of the spinner. Then the support is $S=\\{-2,-1,0,1,2,3\\},$ and the corresponding probabilities are all $\\frac{1}{6}:$\n\n$$\nf(-2)=f(-1)=f(0)=f(1)=f(2)=f(3)=\\frac{1}{6}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =-2\\cdot f(-2)+(-1)\\cdot f(-1)+0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & =-2(\\frac{1}{6})+(-1)(\\frac{1}{6})+0(\\frac{1}{6})+1(\\frac{1}{6})+2(\\frac{1}{6})+3(\\frac{1}{6}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{6}-\\frac{1}{6}+0+\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{2}{6}+\\frac{3}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2-1+0+1+2+3}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-36c5b657-8ae8-52f1-9b50-9850b824e02a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-36c5b657-8ae8-52f1-9b50-9850b824e02a" :answer-field/id #uuid "36c5b657-8ae8-52f1-9b50-9850b824e02a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-e15daab7-6b24-5c89-8928-f0f9fcd1b856" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e15daab7-6b24-5c89-8928-f0f9fcd1b856"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e15daab7-6b24-5c89-8928-f0f9fcd1b856" :answer/id #uuid "e15daab7-6b24-5c89-8928-f0f9fcd1b856" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186357384 :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the spin of the fair spinner. Then the support is $S=\\{-2,-1,1,3,5,6\\},$ and the corresponding probabilities are all $\\frac{1}{6}:$\n\n$$\nf(-2)=f(-1)=f(1)=f(3)=f(5)=f(6)=\\frac{1}{6}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =(-2)\\cdot f(-2)+(-1)\\cdot f(-1)+1\\cdot f(1)+3\\cdot f(3)+5\\cdot f(5)+6\\cdot f(6) \\\\  & =(-2)(\\frac{1}{6})+(-1)(\\frac{1}{6})+1(\\frac{1}{6})+3(\\frac{1}{6})+5(\\frac{1}{6})+6(\\frac{1}{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{-2}{6}+\\frac{-1}{6}+\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{3}{6}+\\frac{5}{6}+\\frac{6}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2-1+1+3+5+6}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{6} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-522d89ff-41d6-50ec-8d1b-a4ada325fbc8" :question/id #uuid "522d89ff-41d6-50ec-8d1b-a4ada325fbc8" :question/math-academy-id "q-83981" :question/problem "A stack contains four cards, where each card is labeled $1$, $4$, $6$, or $9.$ If one card is randomly drawn, what is its expected value?" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the label on a randomly drawn card. Then the support is $S=\\{1,4,6,9\\},$ and the corresponding probabilities are all $\\frac{1}{4}:$\n\n$$\nf(1)=f(4)=f(6)=f(9)=\\frac{1}{4}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot f(1)+4\\cdot f(4)+6\\cdot f(6)+9\\cdot f(9) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{4})+4(\\frac{1}{4})+6(\\frac{1}{4})+9(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{4}{4}+\\frac{6}{4}+\\frac{9}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+4+6+9}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{4} \\\\  & =5\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-850858f3-9f08-5b6d-b191-4d25dc883811"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-850858f3-9f08-5b6d-b191-4d25dc883811" :answer-field/id #uuid "850858f3-9f08-5b6d-b191-4d25dc883811" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5b73964e-ee01-5caf-b596-26a1127dfc1a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f7a0885c-49d2-5c12-bd6c-2ba68d197915" "answer-290464f7-629a-599f-9619-f15eb5786d1b" "answer-5b73964e-ee01-5caf-b596-26a1127dfc1a" "answer-51e0957a-5bf2-56a2-93c7-c85dbc288c19" "answer-9d79ce2e-0688-5dfd-92d7-ae8f08fcc6bc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f7a0885c-49d2-5c12-bd6c-2ba68d197915" :answer/id #uuid "f7a0885c-49d2-5c12-bd6c-2ba68d197915" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-290464f7-629a-599f-9619-f15eb5786d1b" :answer/id #uuid "290464f7-629a-599f-9619-f15eb5786d1b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b73964e-ee01-5caf-b596-26a1127dfc1a" :answer/id #uuid "5b73964e-ee01-5caf-b596-26a1127dfc1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-51e0957a-5bf2-56a2-93c7-c85dbc288c19" :answer/id #uuid "51e0957a-5bf2-56a2-93c7-c85dbc288c19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d79ce2e-0688-5dfd-92d7-ae8f08fcc6bc" :answer/id #uuid "9d79ce2e-0688-5dfd-92d7-ae8f08fcc6bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d66ccea1-6118-5ac8-bad9-91d326fbbfdc" :question/id #uuid "d66ccea1-6118-5ac8-bad9-91d326fbbfdc" :question/math-academy-id "q-5775" :question/problem "What is the expected value of one roll of a seven-sided die?" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the roll of a standard six-sided die. Then the support is $S=\\{1,2,3,4,5,6,7\\},$ and the corresponding probabilities are all $\\frac{1}{7}:$\n\n$$\nf(1)=f(2)=…=f(7)=\\frac{1}{7}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+…+7\\cdot f(7) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{7})+2(\\frac{1}{7})+…+7(\\frac{1}{7}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}+\\frac{2}{7}+…+\\frac{7}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+2+3+4+5+6+7}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{28}{7} \\\\  & =4\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2ec163e0-26a6-57f4-be06-48ae685c5412"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2ec163e0-26a6-57f4-be06-48ae685c5412" :answer-field/id #uuid "2ec163e0-26a6-57f4-be06-48ae685c5412" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5762b6c1-c01c-597b-9835-929afcb6f899" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ae1705d9-17cc-5143-b4de-f594d074c4ba" "answer-5762b6c1-c01c-597b-9835-929afcb6f899" "answer-78fc98f4-275f-5076-bbb7-8cc595a03416" "answer-6f459d6c-f88c-58f8-8c67-ce4a713307e8" "answer-e9e43695-a50c-5db3-a1b5-0d7b31b148a2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae1705d9-17cc-5143-b4de-f594d074c4ba" :answer/id #uuid "ae1705d9-17cc-5143-b4de-f594d074c4ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5762b6c1-c01c-597b-9835-929afcb6f899" :answer/id #uuid "5762b6c1-c01c-597b-9835-929afcb6f899" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78fc98f4-275f-5076-bbb7-8cc595a03416" :answer/id #uuid "78fc98f4-275f-5076-bbb7-8cc595a03416" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6f459d6c-f88c-58f8-8c67-ce4a713307e8" :answer/id #uuid "6f459d6c-f88c-58f8-8c67-ce4a713307e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e9e43695-a50c-5db3-a1b5-0d7b31b148a2" :answer/id #uuid "e9e43695-a50c-5db3-a1b5-0d7b31b148a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-0298a94b-23a5-5b8c-89b1-b11dd1bda638" :question/id #uuid "0298a94b-23a5-5b8c-89b1-b11dd1bda638" :question/math-academy-id "q-89150" :question/problem "What is the expected value of one roll of a four-sided die?" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the roll of a four-sided die. Then the support is $S=\\{1,2,3,4\\},$ and the corresponding probabilities are all $\\frac{1}{4}:$\n\n$$\nf(1)=f(2)=f(3)=f(4)=\\frac{1}{4}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)++3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{4})+2(\\frac{1}{4})+3(\\frac{1}{4})+4(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{2}{4}+\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{4}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+2+3+4}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{4} \\\\  & =2.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-040b322c-582e-5726-82e2-05dc9e18e0aa"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-040b322c-582e-5726-82e2-05dc9e18e0aa" :answer-field/id #uuid "040b322c-582e-5726-82e2-05dc9e18e0aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-df928123-92fc-5c8f-ae4f-3bf6ff6d7789" :answer-field/choices ["answer-45c85e36-fafb-5cd0-bf93-acbfc1d73fee" "answer-68868532-f794-5090-9203-a2b2d0d74f1c" "answer-4188061c-4dfe-5f94-b792-4dca2da6c67e" "answer-df928123-92fc-5c8f-ae4f-3bf6ff6d7789" "answer-b59463e4-063b-5b43-ba22-7b25a136607c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-45c85e36-fafb-5cd0-bf93-acbfc1d73fee" :answer/id #uuid "45c85e36-fafb-5cd0-bf93-acbfc1d73fee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-68868532-f794-5090-9203-a2b2d0d74f1c" :answer/id #uuid "68868532-f794-5090-9203-a2b2d0d74f1c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4188061c-4dfe-5f94-b792-4dca2da6c67e" :answer/id #uuid "4188061c-4dfe-5f94-b792-4dca2da6c67e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-df928123-92fc-5c8f-ae4f-3bf6ff6d7789" :answer/id #uuid "df928123-92fc-5c8f-ae4f-3bf6ff6d7789" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b59463e4-063b-5b43-ba22-7b25a136607c" :answer/id #uuid "b59463e4-063b-5b43-ba22-7b25a136607c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-53e1317a-3ae2-58ac-bb4d-59a740997145" :question/id #uuid "53e1317a-3ae2-58ac-bb4d-59a740997145" :question/math-academy-id "q-127259" :question/problem "The rolls of an unfair octahedral die follow the probability mass function $f(x)$ as shown in the table below. What is the expected value of one roll of the die?\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{3}{32}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{32}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4)+5\\cdot f(5)+6\\cdot f(6) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{8})+2(\\frac{1}{16})+3(\\frac{1}{16})+4(\\frac{3}{32})+5(\\frac{1}{8})+6(\\frac{1}{32})+7(\\frac{1}{4})+8(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}+\\frac{2}{16}+\\frac{3}{16}+\\frac{12}{32}+\\frac{5}{8}+\\frac{6}{32}+\\frac{7}{4}+\\frac{8}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{32}+\\frac{4}{32}+\\frac{6}{32}+\\frac{12}{32}+\\frac{20}{32}+\\frac{6}{32}+\\frac{56}{32}+\\frac{64}{32} \\\\  & =\\frac{4+4+6+12+20+6+56+64}{32} \\\\  & =\\frac{172}{32} \\\\  & =\\frac{43}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-57adae38-47d4-5119-8e1b-753ad3c2f4c1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-57adae38-47d4-5119-8e1b-753ad3c2f4c1" :answer-field/id #uuid "57adae38-47d4-5119-8e1b-753ad3c2f4c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ba66511f-5970-5a6f-9b8a-e517905c7f12" :answer-field/choices ["answer-69532553-7c14-5c9e-8f67-52df69fbcb70" "answer-ba42e326-790d-5ce1-a2d5-97a6580a41b3" "answer-4a55a640-5056-53aa-a01c-37549144e131" "answer-ba66511f-5970-5a6f-9b8a-e517905c7f12" "answer-a4821310-860e-5fda-9174-3a8a5f122a83"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-69532553-7c14-5c9e-8f67-52df69fbcb70" :answer/id #uuid "69532553-7c14-5c9e-8f67-52df69fbcb70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{19}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ba42e326-790d-5ce1-a2d5-97a6580a41b3" :answer/id #uuid "ba42e326-790d-5ce1-a2d5-97a6580a41b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{43}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4a55a640-5056-53aa-a01c-37549144e131" :answer/id #uuid "4a55a640-5056-53aa-a01c-37549144e131" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{43}{32}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ba66511f-5970-5a6f-9b8a-e517905c7f12" :answer/id #uuid "ba66511f-5970-5a6f-9b8a-e517905c7f12" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{43}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a4821310-860e-5fda-9174-3a8a5f122a83" :answer/id #uuid "a4821310-860e-5fda-9174-3a8a5f122a83" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{53}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6f220269-fce2-5308-a544-a882143be2b5" :question/id #uuid "6f220269-fce2-5308-a544-a882143be2b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-337038" :question/problem "The number of heads facing upward after tossing $3$ unfair coins follows the probability mass function $f(x)$ shown in the table below. What is the expected value of the number of heads facing upward after tossing the $3$ coins? Do not round the answer.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{2}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ |\n\n$\\text{E}[X]=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{2}{9})+1(\\frac{1}{3})+2(\\frac{1}{9})+3(\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =0+\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{2}{9}+1 \\\\  & =0+\\frac{3}{9}+\\frac{2}{9}+\\frac{9}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{0+3+2+9}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-eff3eb79-2efb-59dd-8b16-b566385dd9e7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-eff3eb79-2efb-59dd-8b16-b566385dd9e7" :answer-field/id #uuid "eff3eb79-2efb-59dd-8b16-b566385dd9e7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-ee3a7f8d-4e6d-583c-9448-f641c8a25567" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ee3a7f8d-4e6d-583c-9448-f641c8a25567"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ee3a7f8d-4e6d-583c-9448-f641c8a25567" :answer/id #uuid "ee3a7f8d-4e6d-583c-9448-f641c8a25567" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{14}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-dc6b2040-54a4-56f7-9767-230b7779b10f" :question/id #uuid "dc6b2040-54a4-56f7-9767-230b7779b10f" :question/math-academy-id "q-337188" :question/problem "The sum of the outcomes of one roll of two unfair four-sided dice follows the probability mass function $f(x)$ shown in the table below. What is the expected value of the sum of the outcomes for one roll of the two dice?\n\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{3}{40}$ | $\\frac{7}{40}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{20}$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ | $\\frac{1}{20}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n\n$\\text{E}[X]=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4)+5\\cdot f(5) \\\\  & \\,\\,+6\\cdot f(6)+7\\cdot f(7)+8\\cdot f(8) \\\\  & =2(\\frac{3}{40})+3(\\frac{7}{40})+4(\\frac{1}{5})+5(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & \\,\\,+6(\\frac{3}{20})+7(\\frac{1}{10})+8(\\frac{1}{20}) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{40}+\\frac{21}{40}+\\frac{4}{5}+\\frac{5}{4}+\\frac{18}{20}+\\frac{7}{10}+\\frac{8}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{40}+\\frac{21}{40}+\\frac{32}{40}+\\frac{50}{40}+\\frac{36}{40}+\\frac{28}{40}+\\frac{16}{40} \\\\  & =\\frac{6+21+32+50+36+28+16}{40} \\\\  & =\\frac{189}{40} \\\\  & =4.725.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-05e35378-f763-5683-b2ea-96d534b870bf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-05e35378-f763-5683-b2ea-96d534b870bf" :answer-field/id #uuid "05e35378-f763-5683-b2ea-96d534b870bf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-b2b4ec13-aabf-55f7-9a84-533146afb111" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b2b4ec13-aabf-55f7-9a84-533146afb111"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b2b4ec13-aabf-55f7-9a84-533146afb111" :answer/id #uuid "b2b4ec13-aabf-55f7-9a84-533146afb111" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{189}{40}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186370946 :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the value of a randomly drawn bill. Then the support is $S=\\{5,10,20\\}.$\n\nIn the bag there are  $4$ five-dollar bills, $8$ ten-dollar bills and $6$ twenty-dollar bills (eighteen bills in total), so the probabilities are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(5) & =\\frac{4}{18}=\\frac{2}{9} \\\\ P(10) & =\\frac{8}{18}=\\frac{4}{9} \\\\ P(20) & =\\frac{6}{18}=\\frac{3}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =5\\cdot f(5)+10\\cdot f(10)+20\\cdot f(20) \\\\  & =5(\\frac{2}{9})+10(\\frac{4}{9})+20(\\frac{3}{9}) \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{9}+\\frac{40}{9}+\\frac{60}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{10+40+60}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{110}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-ceddea1b-a5cb-5c22-91ab-6571fb7ef388" :question/id #uuid "ceddea1b-a5cb-5c22-91ab-6571fb7ef388" :question/math-academy-id "q-337204" :question/problem "A stack of cards has $2$ cards labeled with four and $6$ cards labeled with ten. If one card is randomly drawn from the stack, what is its expected value?\n\n$\\text{E}[X]=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the value labeled on a randomly drawn card. Then the support is $S=\\{4,10\\}.$\n\nIn the stack there are $2$ cards labeled with four and $6$ cards labeled with ten (eight cards in total), so the probabilities are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(4) & =\\frac{2}{8}=\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ P(10) & =\\frac{6}{8}=\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =4\\cdot f(4)+10\\cdot f(10) \\\\  & =4(\\frac{1}{4})+10(\\frac{3}{4}) \\\\  & =1+\\frac{15}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e295c467-cba5-5269-8303-2482a80e3bd4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e295c467-cba5-5269-8303-2482a80e3bd4" :answer-field/id #uuid "e295c467-cba5-5269-8303-2482a80e3bd4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-f48698d2-8399-5591-8858-d21e6e33a4a6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f48698d2-8399-5591-8858-d21e6e33a4a6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f48698d2-8399-5591-8858-d21e6e33a4a6" :answer/id #uuid "f48698d2-8399-5591-8858-d21e6e33a4a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{17}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-700fffbb-cd63-5378-9077-32b4c2add6e6" :question/id #uuid "700fffbb-cd63-5378-9077-32b4c2add6e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-84067" :question/problem "Several children were asked how many siblings they have. The number of siblings of each child was recorded below. If $X$ is the number of siblings of a randomly selected child, what is the expected value of $X?$\n\n| Number of siblings | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Number of Children | $1$ | $5$ | $3$ | $1$ |" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nWe're given the frequencies of the number of siblings, so we can start by computing the corresponding probabilities. The total number of children is $1+5+3+1=10,$ so the corresponding probabilities are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=0)=f(0) & =\\frac{1}{10} \\\\ P(X=1)=f(1) & =\\frac{5}{10}=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ P(X=2)=f(2) & =\\frac{3}{10} \\\\ P(X=3)=f(3) & =\\frac{1}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe organize these results in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{3}{10}$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ |\n\nNow, summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{1}{10})+1(\\frac{1}{2})+2(\\frac{3}{10})+3(\\frac{1}{10}) \\\\  & =0+\\frac{5}{10}+\\frac{6}{10}+\\frac{3}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{0+5+6+3}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{10} \\\\  & =1.4\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dd980177-3d4f-5c6d-a6cb-2c5b9aaa3857"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dd980177-3d4f-5c6d-a6cb-2c5b9aaa3857" :answer-field/id #uuid "dd980177-3d4f-5c6d-a6cb-2c5b9aaa3857" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5c751fdf-2bec-56e1-938d-e60711842729" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a90215ce-141d-5583-8efd-be89ae2f0bed" "answer-ede15bcc-7345-509e-8ca3-6f297ed035d7" "answer-5c751fdf-2bec-56e1-938d-e60711842729" "answer-6e02a023-2534-54ea-a95d-0e9b379d35c3" "answer-0ce3784e-cee7-5852-894c-71ed7ce007ce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a90215ce-141d-5583-8efd-be89ae2f0bed" :answer/id #uuid "a90215ce-141d-5583-8efd-be89ae2f0bed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ede15bcc-7345-509e-8ca3-6f297ed035d7" :answer/id #uuid "ede15bcc-7345-509e-8ca3-6f297ed035d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5c751fdf-2bec-56e1-938d-e60711842729" :answer/id #uuid "5c751fdf-2bec-56e1-938d-e60711842729" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e02a023-2534-54ea-a95d-0e9b379d35c3" :answer/id #uuid "6e02a023-2534-54ea-a95d-0e9b379d35c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ce3784e-cee7-5852-894c-71ed7ce007ce" :answer/id #uuid "0ce3784e-cee7-5852-894c-71ed7ce007ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-41c4d9f2-fb24-5742-893b-e72bc5478b30" :question/id #uuid "41c4d9f2-fb24-5742-893b-e72bc5478b30" :question/math-academy-id "q-276300" :question/problem "A quality control manager at a warehouse inspects electronic boxes for defective items. The number of faulty items in each box was recorded and summarized below. If $X$ is the number of faulty items in a box, what is the expected value of $X?$\n\n| Number of Boxes | $13$ | $6$ | $4$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Faulty Items | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n\n$\\text{E}[X]=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nWe're given the frequencies of the faulty items, so we can start by computing the corresponding probabilities. The total number of boxes is $13+6+4+2=25,$ so the corresponding probabilities are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=0)=f(0) & =\\frac{13}{25} \\\\ P(X=1)=f(1) & =\\frac{6}{25} \\\\ P(X=2)=f(2) & =\\frac{4}{25} \\\\ P(X=3)=f(3) & =\\frac{2}{25}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe organize these results in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{13}{25}$ | $\\frac{6}{25}$ | $\\frac{4}{25}$ | $\\frac{2}{25}$ |\n\nNow, summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{13}{25})+1(\\frac{6}{25})+2(\\frac{4}{25})+3(\\frac{2}{25}) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{25}+\\frac{8}{25}+\\frac{6}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{6+8+6}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-55e2ebfb-2990-504c-a3b7-16d650b15125"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-55e2ebfb-2990-504c-a3b7-16d650b15125" :answer-field/id #uuid "55e2ebfb-2990-504c-a3b7-16d650b15125" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-a3a5e633-756d-5e3a-8fa9-0ed6225a69ee" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a3a5e633-756d-5e3a-8fa9-0ed6225a69ee"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a3a5e633-756d-5e3a-8fa9-0ed6225a69ee" :answer/id #uuid "a3a5e633-756d-5e3a-8fa9-0ed6225a69ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d599b4ec-9437-5cdd-aa0b-91b4481a6586" :question/id #uuid "d599b4ec-9437-5cdd-aa0b-91b4481a6586" :question/math-academy-id "q-89157" :question/problem "Several households were asked the number of children that lived there. The number of children in each was recorded below. If $X$ is the number of children that live at a randomly selected household, what is the expected value of $X?$\n\n| Number of Children | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Number of Households | $6$ | $9$ | $6$ | $3$ |" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nWe're given the frequencies of the number of childen, so we can start by computing the corresponding probabilities. The total number of households is $3+9+6+6=24,$ so the corresponding probabilities are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=1)=f(1) & =\\frac{6}{24}=\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ P(X=2)=f(2) & =\\frac{9}{24}=\\frac{3}{8} \\\\ P(X=3)=f(3) & =\\frac{6}{24}=\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ P(X=4)=f(4) & =\\frac{3}{24}=\\frac{1}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe organize these results in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n\nNow, summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{4})+2(\\frac{3}{8})+3(\\frac{1}{4})+4(\\frac{1}{8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{2}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+3+3+2}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4} \\\\  & =2.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-618772c4-492e-57e3-9e76-dc9f3ada338c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-618772c4-492e-57e3-9e76-dc9f3ada338c" :answer-field/id #uuid "618772c4-492e-57e3-9e76-dc9f3ada338c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2a02737d-84cc-5b65-a38a-d8f95f1427b0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c5540b63-e212-55cb-b7a9-7c7a2846f551" "answer-7566e7ed-5b8d-55f6-bcd8-3e0711ba276d" "answer-c95ceba2-efcb-54f1-bc4a-d6b2a95fef1a" "answer-2a02737d-84cc-5b65-a38a-d8f95f1427b0" "answer-93cd1bc1-ffd4-50f6-955c-6bee087d74b2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c5540b63-e212-55cb-b7a9-7c7a2846f551" :answer/id #uuid "c5540b63-e212-55cb-b7a9-7c7a2846f551" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7566e7ed-5b8d-55f6-bcd8-3e0711ba276d" :answer/id #uuid "7566e7ed-5b8d-55f6-bcd8-3e0711ba276d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.75" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c95ceba2-efcb-54f1-bc4a-d6b2a95fef1a" :answer/id #uuid "c95ceba2-efcb-54f1-bc4a-d6b2a95fef1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2a02737d-84cc-5b65-a38a-d8f95f1427b0" :answer/id #uuid "2a02737d-84cc-5b65-a38a-d8f95f1427b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-93cd1bc1-ffd4-50f6-955c-6bee087d74b2" :answer/id #uuid "93cd1bc1-ffd4-50f6-955c-6bee087d74b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-068e9bc7-6f46-5ac9-a057-d5f4aa9a8aeb" :question/id #uuid "068e9bc7-6f46-5ac9-a057-d5f4aa9a8aeb" :question/math-academy-id "q-127818" :question/problem "One way to bet in roulette is to place $\\$1$ on a single number. If the ball lands on that number, the player wins $\\$35.$ If the ball lands on any of the other $37$ slots, the player doesn't win. What is the expected profit, rounded to the nearest dollar, for a player who plays one hundred games on number $12$ in a row?" :question/worked-solution "First of all, profit is revenue minus cost, or in our case, winnings minus cost. So, once we have found the expected winnings after one hundred games, we need to subtract $100\\cdot 1=100$ dollars to account for the price of playing.\n\nNow, let's find the expected winnings and summarize them in a table. If $W$ is the winnings (in dollars) on a single game, and $f(w)$ is the probability mass function for $W,$ then we have the following:\n\n| $f(w)$ | $\\frac{1}{38}$ | $\\frac{37}{38}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $w$ | $35$ | $0$ |\n\nThe expected value of $W$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[W] & =35\\cdot f(35)+0\\cdot f(0) \\\\  & =35(\\frac{1}{38})+0(\\frac{37}{38}) \\\\  & =\\frac{35}{38} \\\\  & ≈0.92.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis represents the expected winnings for a single game. So, the expected winnings for $100$ games  on number $12$ is\n\n$$\n100\\cdot \\text{E}[W]=100\\cdot (0.92)=92.\n$$\n\nNow, subtracting the $100$ dollars paid to play, we get that the expected profit (in dollars) is\n\n$$\nE[p]=92-100=-8.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-53865da6-8e44-5bb9-8d40-4d2805caf8a7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-53865da6-8e44-5bb9-8d40-4d2805caf8a7" :answer-field/id #uuid "53865da6-8e44-5bb9-8d40-4d2805caf8a7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b1e0eb6a-bd70-5f35-a14d-f4f095208cc4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1bec36d6-dfb7-5749-9664-f7f73dc25b79" "answer-2e9bbeaf-98e6-558c-81d6-d0813fc9f4ac" "answer-b1e0eb6a-bd70-5f35-a14d-f4f095208cc4" "answer-59a5f4bc-a0cc-5d8a-b1c9-87ca178ebcf7" "answer-8e4ee2a5-d371-5586-98ed-838864441766"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1bec36d6-dfb7-5749-9664-f7f73dc25b79" :answer/id #uuid "1bec36d6-dfb7-5749-9664-f7f73dc25b79" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-\\$10$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2e9bbeaf-98e6-558c-81d6-d0813fc9f4ac" :answer/id #uuid "2e9bbeaf-98e6-558c-81d6-d0813fc9f4ac" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-\\$19$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b1e0eb6a-bd70-5f35-a14d-f4f095208cc4" :answer/id #uuid "b1e0eb6a-bd70-5f35-a14d-f4f095208cc4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-\\$8$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-59a5f4bc-a0cc-5d8a-b1c9-87ca178ebcf7" :answer/id #uuid "59a5f4bc-a0cc-5d8a-b1c9-87ca178ebcf7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\$7$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e4ee2a5-d371-5586-98ed-838864441766" :answer/id #uuid "8e4ee2a5-d371-5586-98ed-838864441766" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\$9$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-267e0e90-b604-5e86-ad43-795951237ad2" :question/id #uuid "267e0e90-b604-5e86-ad43-795951237ad2" :question/math-academy-id "q-337346" :question/problem "One way to bet in roulette is to place $\\$2$ on a single number. If the ball lands on that number, the player wins $\\$70.$ If the ball lands on any of the other $37$ slots, the player doesn't win. What is the expected profit, rounded to the nearest dollar, for a player who plays one hundred games on number $8$ in a row?\n\nThe expected profit in dollars is $E(p)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First of all, profit is revenue minus cost, or in our case, winnings minus cost. So, once we have found the expected winnings after one hundred games, we need to subtract $100\\cdot 2=200$ dollars to account for the price of playing.\n\nNow, let's find the expected winnings and summarize them in a table. If $W$ is the winnings (in dollars) on a single game, and $f(w)$ is the probability mass function for $W,$ then we have the following:\n\n| $f(w)$ | $\\frac{1}{38}$ | $\\frac{37}{38}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $w$ | $70$ | $0$ |\n\nThe expected value of $W$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[W] & =70\\cdot f(70)+0\\cdot f(0) \\\\  & =70(\\frac{1}{38})+0(\\frac{37}{38}) \\\\  & =\\frac{70}{38} \\\\  & ≈1.84.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis represents the expected winnings for a single game. So, the expected winnings for $100$ games on number $8$ is\n\n$$\n100\\cdot \\text{E}[W]=100\\cdot (1.84)=184.\n$$\n\nNow, subtracting the $200$ dollars paid to play, we get that the expected profit (in dollars) is\n\n$$\nE[p]=184-200=-16.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4197adf1-104f-52af-a2fe-ce58ae6658aa"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4197adf1-104f-52af-a2fe-ce58ae6658aa" :answer-field/id #uuid "4197adf1-104f-52af-a2fe-ce58ae6658aa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-f39199e8-353c-5632-85b5-146e5d346bc2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f39199e8-353c-5632-85b5-146e5d346bc2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f39199e8-353c-5632-85b5-146e5d346bc2" :answer/id #uuid "f39199e8-353c-5632-85b5-146e5d346bc2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083425 :activity/expected-seconds 960.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}] "assertions" [["question-9cdf7c4f-4409-57f0-b1eb-dca5de834f65" :question/id #uuid "9cdf7c4f-4409-57f0-b1eb-dca5de834f65"] ["question-9cdf7c4f-4409-57f0-b1eb-dca5de834f65" :question/math-academy-id "q-276297"] ["question-9cdf7c4f-4409-57f0-b1eb-dca5de834f65" :question/problem "A fair spinner has six sides labeled with the numbers $-2,$ $-1,$ $0,$ $1,$ $2,$ and $3.$ If the spinner is spun, what is the expected value of the outcome?\n\n$\\text{E}[X]=$\n{{field-1}}"] ["question-9cdf7c4f-4409-57f0-b1eb-dca5de834f65" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the outcome of the spinner. Then the support is $S=\\{-2,-1,0,1,2,3\\},$ and the corresponding probabilities are all $\\frac{1}{6}:$\n\n$$\nf(-2)=f(-1)=f(0)=f(1)=f(2)=f(3)=\\frac{1}{6}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =-2\\cdot f(-2)+(-1)\\cdot f(-1)+0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & =-2(\\frac{1}{6})+(-1)(\\frac{1}{6})+0(\\frac{1}{6})+1(\\frac{1}{6})+2(\\frac{1}{6})+3(\\frac{1}{6}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{6}-\\frac{1}{6}+0+\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{2}{6}+\\frac{3}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2-1+0+1+2+3}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-9cdf7c4f-4409-57f0-b1eb-dca5de834f65" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-36c5b657-8ae8-52f1-9b50-9850b824e02a" :answer-field/id #uuid "36c5b657-8ae8-52f1-9b50-9850b824e02a"] ["answer-e15daab7-6b24-5c89-8928-f0f9fcd1b856" :answer/id #uuid "e15daab7-6b24-5c89-8928-f0f9fcd1b856"] ["answer-e15daab7-6b24-5c89-8928-f0f9fcd1b856" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e15daab7-6b24-5c89-8928-f0f9fcd1b856" :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["answer-field-36c5b657-8ae8-52f1-9b50-9850b824e02a" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-36c5b657-8ae8-52f1-9b50-9850b824e02a" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-36c5b657-8ae8-52f1-9b50-9850b824e02a" :answer-field/correct "answer-e15daab7-6b24-5c89-8928-f0f9fcd1b856"] ["answer-field-36c5b657-8ae8-52f1-9b50-9850b824e02a" :answer-field/choices "answer-e15daab7-6b24-5c89-8928-f0f9fcd1b856"] ["question-9cdf7c4f-4409-57f0-b1eb-dca5de834f65" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-36c5b657-8ae8-52f1-9b50-9850b824e02a"] [17592186083272 :knowledge-point/questions "question-9cdf7c4f-4409-57f0-b1eb-dca5de834f65"] [17592186357384 :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the spin of the fair spinner. Then the support is $S=\\{-2,-1,1,3,5,6\\},$ and the corresponding probabilities are all $\\frac{1}{6}:$\n\n$$\nf(-2)=f(-1)=f(1)=f(3)=f(5)=f(6)=\\frac{1}{6}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =(-2)\\cdot f(-2)+(-1)\\cdot f(-1)+1\\cdot f(1)+3\\cdot f(3)+5\\cdot f(5)+6\\cdot f(6) \\\\  & =(-2)(\\frac{1}{6})+(-1)(\\frac{1}{6})+1(\\frac{1}{6})+3(\\frac{1}{6})+5(\\frac{1}{6})+6(\\frac{1}{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{-2}{6}+\\frac{-1}{6}+\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{3}{6}+\\frac{5}{6}+\\frac{6}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2-1+1+3+5+6}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{6} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-522d89ff-41d6-50ec-8d1b-a4ada325fbc8" :question/id #uuid "522d89ff-41d6-50ec-8d1b-a4ada325fbc8"] ["question-522d89ff-41d6-50ec-8d1b-a4ada325fbc8" :question/math-academy-id "q-83981"] ["question-522d89ff-41d6-50ec-8d1b-a4ada325fbc8" :question/problem "A stack contains four cards, where each card is labeled $1$, $4$, $6$, or $9.$ If one card is randomly drawn, what is its expected value?"] ["question-522d89ff-41d6-50ec-8d1b-a4ada325fbc8" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the label on a randomly drawn card. Then the support is $S=\\{1,4,6,9\\},$ and the corresponding probabilities are all $\\frac{1}{4}:$\n\n$$\nf(1)=f(4)=f(6)=f(9)=\\frac{1}{4}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot f(1)+4\\cdot f(4)+6\\cdot f(6)+9\\cdot f(9) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{4})+4(\\frac{1}{4})+6(\\frac{1}{4})+9(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{4}{4}+\\frac{6}{4}+\\frac{9}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+4+6+9}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{4} \\\\  & =5\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-522d89ff-41d6-50ec-8d1b-a4ada325fbc8" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-850858f3-9f08-5b6d-b191-4d25dc883811" :answer-field/id #uuid "850858f3-9f08-5b6d-b191-4d25dc883811"] ["answer-f7a0885c-49d2-5c12-bd6c-2ba68d197915" :answer/id #uuid "f7a0885c-49d2-5c12-bd6c-2ba68d197915"] ["answer-f7a0885c-49d2-5c12-bd6c-2ba68d197915" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f7a0885c-49d2-5c12-bd6c-2ba68d197915" :answer/value "4"] ["answer-290464f7-629a-599f-9619-f15eb5786d1b" :answer/id #uuid "290464f7-629a-599f-9619-f15eb5786d1b"] ["answer-290464f7-629a-599f-9619-f15eb5786d1b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-290464f7-629a-599f-9619-f15eb5786d1b" :answer/value "4.5"] ["answer-5b73964e-ee01-5caf-b596-26a1127dfc1a" :answer/id #uuid "5b73964e-ee01-5caf-b596-26a1127dfc1a"] ["answer-5b73964e-ee01-5caf-b596-26a1127dfc1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-5b73964e-ee01-5caf-b596-26a1127dfc1a" :answer/value "5"] ["answer-51e0957a-5bf2-56a2-93c7-c85dbc288c19" :answer/id #uuid "51e0957a-5bf2-56a2-93c7-c85dbc288c19"] ["answer-51e0957a-5bf2-56a2-93c7-c85dbc288c19" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-51e0957a-5bf2-56a2-93c7-c85dbc288c19" :answer/value "5.5"] ["answer-9d79ce2e-0688-5dfd-92d7-ae8f08fcc6bc" :answer/id #uuid "9d79ce2e-0688-5dfd-92d7-ae8f08fcc6bc"] ["answer-9d79ce2e-0688-5dfd-92d7-ae8f08fcc6bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-9d79ce2e-0688-5dfd-92d7-ae8f08fcc6bc" :answer/value "6"] ["answer-field-850858f3-9f08-5b6d-b191-4d25dc883811" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-850858f3-9f08-5b6d-b191-4d25dc883811" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-850858f3-9f08-5b6d-b191-4d25dc883811" :answer-field/correct "answer-5b73964e-ee01-5caf-b596-26a1127dfc1a"] ["answer-field-850858f3-9f08-5b6d-b191-4d25dc883811" :answer-field/choices "answer-f7a0885c-49d2-5c12-bd6c-2ba68d197915"] ["answer-field-850858f3-9f08-5b6d-b191-4d25dc883811" :answer-field/choices "answer-290464f7-629a-599f-9619-f15eb5786d1b"] ["answer-field-850858f3-9f08-5b6d-b191-4d25dc883811" :answer-field/choices "answer-5b73964e-ee01-5caf-b596-26a1127dfc1a"] ["answer-field-850858f3-9f08-5b6d-b191-4d25dc883811" :answer-field/choices "answer-51e0957a-5bf2-56a2-93c7-c85dbc288c19"] ["answer-field-850858f3-9f08-5b6d-b191-4d25dc883811" :answer-field/choices "answer-9d79ce2e-0688-5dfd-92d7-ae8f08fcc6bc"] ["question-522d89ff-41d6-50ec-8d1b-a4ada325fbc8" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-850858f3-9f08-5b6d-b191-4d25dc883811"] [17592186083272 :knowledge-point/questions "question-522d89ff-41d6-50ec-8d1b-a4ada325fbc8"] ["question-d66ccea1-6118-5ac8-bad9-91d326fbbfdc" :question/id #uuid "d66ccea1-6118-5ac8-bad9-91d326fbbfdc"] ["question-d66ccea1-6118-5ac8-bad9-91d326fbbfdc" :question/math-academy-id "q-5775"] ["question-d66ccea1-6118-5ac8-bad9-91d326fbbfdc" :question/problem "What is the expected value of one roll of a seven-sided die?"] ["question-d66ccea1-6118-5ac8-bad9-91d326fbbfdc" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the roll of a standard six-sided die. Then the support is $S=\\{1,2,3,4,5,6,7\\},$ and the corresponding probabilities are all $\\frac{1}{7}:$\n\n$$\nf(1)=f(2)=…=f(7)=\\frac{1}{7}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+…+7\\cdot f(7) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{7})+2(\\frac{1}{7})+…+7(\\frac{1}{7}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}+\\frac{2}{7}+…+\\frac{7}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+2+3+4+5+6+7}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{28}{7} \\\\  & =4\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-d66ccea1-6118-5ac8-bad9-91d326fbbfdc" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-2ec163e0-26a6-57f4-be06-48ae685c5412" :answer-field/id #uuid "2ec163e0-26a6-57f4-be06-48ae685c5412"] ["answer-ae1705d9-17cc-5143-b4de-f594d074c4ba" :answer/id #uuid "ae1705d9-17cc-5143-b4de-f594d074c4ba"] ["answer-ae1705d9-17cc-5143-b4de-f594d074c4ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ae1705d9-17cc-5143-b4de-f594d074c4ba" :answer/value "3.5"] ["answer-5762b6c1-c01c-597b-9835-929afcb6f899" :answer/id #uuid "5762b6c1-c01c-597b-9835-929afcb6f899"] ["answer-5762b6c1-c01c-597b-9835-929afcb6f899" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-5762b6c1-c01c-597b-9835-929afcb6f899" :answer/value "4"] ["answer-78fc98f4-275f-5076-bbb7-8cc595a03416" :answer/id #uuid "78fc98f4-275f-5076-bbb7-8cc595a03416"] ["answer-78fc98f4-275f-5076-bbb7-8cc595a03416" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-78fc98f4-275f-5076-bbb7-8cc595a03416" :answer/value "4.5"] ["answer-6f459d6c-f88c-58f8-8c67-ce4a713307e8" :answer/id #uuid "6f459d6c-f88c-58f8-8c67-ce4a713307e8"] ["answer-6f459d6c-f88c-58f8-8c67-ce4a713307e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-6f459d6c-f88c-58f8-8c67-ce4a713307e8" :answer/value "5"] ["answer-e9e43695-a50c-5db3-a1b5-0d7b31b148a2" :answer/id #uuid "e9e43695-a50c-5db3-a1b5-0d7b31b148a2"] ["answer-e9e43695-a50c-5db3-a1b5-0d7b31b148a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e9e43695-a50c-5db3-a1b5-0d7b31b148a2" :answer/value "5.5"] ["answer-field-2ec163e0-26a6-57f4-be06-48ae685c5412" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-2ec163e0-26a6-57f4-be06-48ae685c5412" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-2ec163e0-26a6-57f4-be06-48ae685c5412" :answer-field/correct "answer-5762b6c1-c01c-597b-9835-929afcb6f899"] ["answer-field-2ec163e0-26a6-57f4-be06-48ae685c5412" :answer-field/choices "answer-ae1705d9-17cc-5143-b4de-f594d074c4ba"] ["answer-field-2ec163e0-26a6-57f4-be06-48ae685c5412" :answer-field/choices "answer-5762b6c1-c01c-597b-9835-929afcb6f899"] ["answer-field-2ec163e0-26a6-57f4-be06-48ae685c5412" :answer-field/choices "answer-78fc98f4-275f-5076-bbb7-8cc595a03416"] ["answer-field-2ec163e0-26a6-57f4-be06-48ae685c5412" :answer-field/choices "answer-6f459d6c-f88c-58f8-8c67-ce4a713307e8"] ["answer-field-2ec163e0-26a6-57f4-be06-48ae685c5412" :answer-field/choices "answer-e9e43695-a50c-5db3-a1b5-0d7b31b148a2"] ["question-d66ccea1-6118-5ac8-bad9-91d326fbbfdc" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-2ec163e0-26a6-57f4-be06-48ae685c5412"] [17592186083272 :knowledge-point/questions "question-d66ccea1-6118-5ac8-bad9-91d326fbbfdc"] ["question-0298a94b-23a5-5b8c-89b1-b11dd1bda638" :question/id #uuid "0298a94b-23a5-5b8c-89b1-b11dd1bda638"] ["question-0298a94b-23a5-5b8c-89b1-b11dd1bda638" :question/math-academy-id "q-89150"] ["question-0298a94b-23a5-5b8c-89b1-b11dd1bda638" :question/problem "What is the expected value of one roll of a four-sided die?"] ["question-0298a94b-23a5-5b8c-89b1-b11dd1bda638" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the roll of a four-sided die. Then the support is $S=\\{1,2,3,4\\},$ and the corresponding probabilities are all $\\frac{1}{4}:$\n\n$$\nf(1)=f(2)=f(3)=f(4)=\\frac{1}{4}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)++3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{4})+2(\\frac{1}{4})+3(\\frac{1}{4})+4(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{2}{4}+\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{4}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+2+3+4}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{4} \\\\  & =2.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-0298a94b-23a5-5b8c-89b1-b11dd1bda638" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-040b322c-582e-5726-82e2-05dc9e18e0aa" :answer-field/id #uuid "040b322c-582e-5726-82e2-05dc9e18e0aa"] ["answer-45c85e36-fafb-5cd0-bf93-acbfc1d73fee" :answer/id #uuid "45c85e36-fafb-5cd0-bf93-acbfc1d73fee"] ["answer-45c85e36-fafb-5cd0-bf93-acbfc1d73fee" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-45c85e36-fafb-5cd0-bf93-acbfc1d73fee" :answer/value "1"] ["answer-68868532-f794-5090-9203-a2b2d0d74f1c" :answer/id #uuid "68868532-f794-5090-9203-a2b2d0d74f1c"] ["answer-68868532-f794-5090-9203-a2b2d0d74f1c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-68868532-f794-5090-9203-a2b2d0d74f1c" :answer/value "1.5"] ["answer-4188061c-4dfe-5f94-b792-4dca2da6c67e" :answer/id #uuid "4188061c-4dfe-5f94-b792-4dca2da6c67e"] ["answer-4188061c-4dfe-5f94-b792-4dca2da6c67e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-4188061c-4dfe-5f94-b792-4dca2da6c67e" :answer/value "2"] ["answer-df928123-92fc-5c8f-ae4f-3bf6ff6d7789" :answer/id #uuid "df928123-92fc-5c8f-ae4f-3bf6ff6d7789"] ["answer-df928123-92fc-5c8f-ae4f-3bf6ff6d7789" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-df928123-92fc-5c8f-ae4f-3bf6ff6d7789" :answer/value "2.5"] ["answer-b59463e4-063b-5b43-ba22-7b25a136607c" :answer/id #uuid "b59463e4-063b-5b43-ba22-7b25a136607c"] ["answer-b59463e4-063b-5b43-ba22-7b25a136607c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-b59463e4-063b-5b43-ba22-7b25a136607c" :answer/value "3"] ["answer-field-040b322c-582e-5726-82e2-05dc9e18e0aa" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-040b322c-582e-5726-82e2-05dc9e18e0aa" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-040b322c-582e-5726-82e2-05dc9e18e0aa" :answer-field/correct "answer-df928123-92fc-5c8f-ae4f-3bf6ff6d7789"] ["answer-field-040b322c-582e-5726-82e2-05dc9e18e0aa" :answer-field/choices "answer-45c85e36-fafb-5cd0-bf93-acbfc1d73fee"] ["answer-field-040b322c-582e-5726-82e2-05dc9e18e0aa" :answer-field/choices "answer-68868532-f794-5090-9203-a2b2d0d74f1c"] ["answer-field-040b322c-582e-5726-82e2-05dc9e18e0aa" :answer-field/choices "answer-4188061c-4dfe-5f94-b792-4dca2da6c67e"] ["answer-field-040b322c-582e-5726-82e2-05dc9e18e0aa" :answer-field/choices "answer-df928123-92fc-5c8f-ae4f-3bf6ff6d7789"] ["answer-field-040b322c-582e-5726-82e2-05dc9e18e0aa" :answer-field/choices "answer-b59463e4-063b-5b43-ba22-7b25a136607c"] ["question-0298a94b-23a5-5b8c-89b1-b11dd1bda638" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-040b322c-582e-5726-82e2-05dc9e18e0aa"] [17592186083272 :knowledge-point/questions "question-0298a94b-23a5-5b8c-89b1-b11dd1bda638"] ["question-53e1317a-3ae2-58ac-bb4d-59a740997145" :question/id #uuid "53e1317a-3ae2-58ac-bb4d-59a740997145"] ["question-53e1317a-3ae2-58ac-bb4d-59a740997145" :question/math-academy-id "q-127259"] ["question-53e1317a-3ae2-58ac-bb4d-59a740997145" :question/problem "The rolls of an unfair octahedral die follow the probability mass function $f(x)$ as shown in the table below. What is the expected value of one roll of the die?\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{3}{32}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{32}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |"] ["question-53e1317a-3ae2-58ac-bb4d-59a740997145" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4)+5\\cdot f(5)+6\\cdot f(6) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{8})+2(\\frac{1}{16})+3(\\frac{1}{16})+4(\\frac{3}{32})+5(\\frac{1}{8})+6(\\frac{1}{32})+7(\\frac{1}{4})+8(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}+\\frac{2}{16}+\\frac{3}{16}+\\frac{12}{32}+\\frac{5}{8}+\\frac{6}{32}+\\frac{7}{4}+\\frac{8}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{32}+\\frac{4}{32}+\\frac{6}{32}+\\frac{12}{32}+\\frac{20}{32}+\\frac{6}{32}+\\frac{56}{32}+\\frac{64}{32} \\\\  & =\\frac{4+4+6+12+20+6+56+64}{32} \\\\  & =\\frac{172}{32} \\\\  & =\\frac{43}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-53e1317a-3ae2-58ac-bb4d-59a740997145" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-57adae38-47d4-5119-8e1b-753ad3c2f4c1" :answer-field/id #uuid "57adae38-47d4-5119-8e1b-753ad3c2f4c1"] ["answer-69532553-7c14-5c9e-8f67-52df69fbcb70" :answer/id #uuid "69532553-7c14-5c9e-8f67-52df69fbcb70"] ["answer-69532553-7c14-5c9e-8f67-52df69fbcb70" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-69532553-7c14-5c9e-8f67-52df69fbcb70" :answer/value "\\frac{19}{8}"] ["answer-ba42e326-790d-5ce1-a2d5-97a6580a41b3" :answer/id #uuid "ba42e326-790d-5ce1-a2d5-97a6580a41b3"] ["answer-ba42e326-790d-5ce1-a2d5-97a6580a41b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ba42e326-790d-5ce1-a2d5-97a6580a41b3" :answer/value "\\frac{43}{16}"] ["answer-4a55a640-5056-53aa-a01c-37549144e131" :answer/id #uuid "4a55a640-5056-53aa-a01c-37549144e131"] ["answer-4a55a640-5056-53aa-a01c-37549144e131" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-4a55a640-5056-53aa-a01c-37549144e131" :answer/value "\\frac{43}{32}"] ["answer-ba66511f-5970-5a6f-9b8a-e517905c7f12" :answer/id #uuid "ba66511f-5970-5a6f-9b8a-e517905c7f12"] ["answer-ba66511f-5970-5a6f-9b8a-e517905c7f12" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ba66511f-5970-5a6f-9b8a-e517905c7f12" :answer/value "\\frac{43}{8}"] ["answer-a4821310-860e-5fda-9174-3a8a5f122a83" :answer/id #uuid "a4821310-860e-5fda-9174-3a8a5f122a83"] ["answer-a4821310-860e-5fda-9174-3a8a5f122a83" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a4821310-860e-5fda-9174-3a8a5f122a83" :answer/value "\\frac{53}{8}"] ["answer-field-57adae38-47d4-5119-8e1b-753ad3c2f4c1" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-57adae38-47d4-5119-8e1b-753ad3c2f4c1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-57adae38-47d4-5119-8e1b-753ad3c2f4c1" :answer-field/correct "answer-ba66511f-5970-5a6f-9b8a-e517905c7f12"] ["answer-field-57adae38-47d4-5119-8e1b-753ad3c2f4c1" :answer-field/choices "answer-69532553-7c14-5c9e-8f67-52df69fbcb70"] ["answer-field-57adae38-47d4-5119-8e1b-753ad3c2f4c1" :answer-field/choices "answer-ba42e326-790d-5ce1-a2d5-97a6580a41b3"] ["answer-field-57adae38-47d4-5119-8e1b-753ad3c2f4c1" :answer-field/choices "answer-4a55a640-5056-53aa-a01c-37549144e131"] ["answer-field-57adae38-47d4-5119-8e1b-753ad3c2f4c1" :answer-field/choices "answer-ba66511f-5970-5a6f-9b8a-e517905c7f12"] ["answer-field-57adae38-47d4-5119-8e1b-753ad3c2f4c1" :answer-field/choices "answer-a4821310-860e-5fda-9174-3a8a5f122a83"] ["question-53e1317a-3ae2-58ac-bb4d-59a740997145" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-57adae38-47d4-5119-8e1b-753ad3c2f4c1"] [17592186083308 :knowledge-point/questions "question-53e1317a-3ae2-58ac-bb4d-59a740997145"] ["question-6f220269-fce2-5308-a544-a882143be2b5" :question/id #uuid "6f220269-fce2-5308-a544-a882143be2b5"] ["question-6f220269-fce2-5308-a544-a882143be2b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-337038"] ["question-6f220269-fce2-5308-a544-a882143be2b5" :question/problem "The number of heads facing upward after tossing $3$ unfair coins follows the probability mass function $f(x)$ shown in the table below. What is the expected value of the number of heads facing upward after tossing the $3$ coins? Do not round the answer.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{2}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ |\n\n$\\text{E}[X]=$\n{{field-1}}"] ["question-6f220269-fce2-5308-a544-a882143be2b5" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{2}{9})+1(\\frac{1}{3})+2(\\frac{1}{9})+3(\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =0+\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{2}{9}+1 \\\\  & =0+\\frac{3}{9}+\\frac{2}{9}+\\frac{9}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{0+3+2+9}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-6f220269-fce2-5308-a544-a882143be2b5" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-eff3eb79-2efb-59dd-8b16-b566385dd9e7" :answer-field/id #uuid "eff3eb79-2efb-59dd-8b16-b566385dd9e7"] ["answer-ee3a7f8d-4e6d-583c-9448-f641c8a25567" :answer/id #uuid "ee3a7f8d-4e6d-583c-9448-f641c8a25567"] ["answer-ee3a7f8d-4e6d-583c-9448-f641c8a25567" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ee3a7f8d-4e6d-583c-9448-f641c8a25567" :answer/value "\\frac{14}{9}"] ["answer-field-eff3eb79-2efb-59dd-8b16-b566385dd9e7" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-eff3eb79-2efb-59dd-8b16-b566385dd9e7" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-eff3eb79-2efb-59dd-8b16-b566385dd9e7" :answer-field/correct "answer-ee3a7f8d-4e6d-583c-9448-f641c8a25567"] ["answer-field-eff3eb79-2efb-59dd-8b16-b566385dd9e7" :answer-field/choices "answer-ee3a7f8d-4e6d-583c-9448-f641c8a25567"] ["question-6f220269-fce2-5308-a544-a882143be2b5" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-eff3eb79-2efb-59dd-8b16-b566385dd9e7"] [17592186083308 :knowledge-point/questions "question-6f220269-fce2-5308-a544-a882143be2b5"] ["question-dc6b2040-54a4-56f7-9767-230b7779b10f" :question/id #uuid "dc6b2040-54a4-56f7-9767-230b7779b10f"] ["question-dc6b2040-54a4-56f7-9767-230b7779b10f" :question/math-academy-id "q-337188"] ["question-dc6b2040-54a4-56f7-9767-230b7779b10f" :question/problem "The sum of the outcomes of one roll of two unfair four-sided dice follows the probability mass function $f(x)$ shown in the table below. What is the expected value of the sum of the outcomes for one roll of the two dice?\n\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{3}{40}$ | $\\frac{7}{40}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{20}$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ | $\\frac{1}{20}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n\n$\\text{E}[X]=$\n{{field-1}}"] ["question-dc6b2040-54a4-56f7-9767-230b7779b10f" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4)+5\\cdot f(5) \\\\  & \\,\\,+6\\cdot f(6)+7\\cdot f(7)+8\\cdot f(8) \\\\  & =2(\\frac{3}{40})+3(\\frac{7}{40})+4(\\frac{1}{5})+5(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & \\,\\,+6(\\frac{3}{20})+7(\\frac{1}{10})+8(\\frac{1}{20}) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{40}+\\frac{21}{40}+\\frac{4}{5}+\\frac{5}{4}+\\frac{18}{20}+\\frac{7}{10}+\\frac{8}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{40}+\\frac{21}{40}+\\frac{32}{40}+\\frac{50}{40}+\\frac{36}{40}+\\frac{28}{40}+\\frac{16}{40} \\\\  & =\\frac{6+21+32+50+36+28+16}{40} \\\\  & =\\frac{189}{40} \\\\  & =4.725.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-dc6b2040-54a4-56f7-9767-230b7779b10f" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-05e35378-f763-5683-b2ea-96d534b870bf" :answer-field/id #uuid "05e35378-f763-5683-b2ea-96d534b870bf"] ["answer-b2b4ec13-aabf-55f7-9a84-533146afb111" :answer/id #uuid "b2b4ec13-aabf-55f7-9a84-533146afb111"] ["answer-b2b4ec13-aabf-55f7-9a84-533146afb111" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-b2b4ec13-aabf-55f7-9a84-533146afb111" :answer/value "\\frac{189}{40}"] ["answer-field-05e35378-f763-5683-b2ea-96d534b870bf" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-05e35378-f763-5683-b2ea-96d534b870bf" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-05e35378-f763-5683-b2ea-96d534b870bf" :answer-field/correct "answer-b2b4ec13-aabf-55f7-9a84-533146afb111"] ["answer-field-05e35378-f763-5683-b2ea-96d534b870bf" :answer-field/choices "answer-b2b4ec13-aabf-55f7-9a84-533146afb111"] ["question-dc6b2040-54a4-56f7-9767-230b7779b10f" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-05e35378-f763-5683-b2ea-96d534b870bf"] [17592186083308 :knowledge-point/questions "question-dc6b2040-54a4-56f7-9767-230b7779b10f"] [17592186370946 :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the value of a randomly drawn bill. Then the support is $S=\\{5,10,20\\}.$\n\nIn the bag there are  $4$ five-dollar bills, $8$ ten-dollar bills and $6$ twenty-dollar bills (eighteen bills in total), so the probabilities are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(5) & =\\frac{4}{18}=\\frac{2}{9} \\\\ P(10) & =\\frac{8}{18}=\\frac{4}{9} \\\\ P(20) & =\\frac{6}{18}=\\frac{3}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =5\\cdot f(5)+10\\cdot f(10)+20\\cdot f(20) \\\\  & =5(\\frac{2}{9})+10(\\frac{4}{9})+20(\\frac{3}{9}) \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{9}+\\frac{40}{9}+\\frac{60}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{10+40+60}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{110}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-ceddea1b-a5cb-5c22-91ab-6571fb7ef388" :question/id #uuid "ceddea1b-a5cb-5c22-91ab-6571fb7ef388"] ["question-ceddea1b-a5cb-5c22-91ab-6571fb7ef388" :question/math-academy-id "q-337204"] ["question-ceddea1b-a5cb-5c22-91ab-6571fb7ef388" :question/problem "A stack of cards has $2$ cards labeled with four and $6$ cards labeled with ten. If one card is randomly drawn from the stack, what is its expected value?\n\n$\\text{E}[X]=$\n{{field-1}}"] ["question-ceddea1b-a5cb-5c22-91ab-6571fb7ef388" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the value labeled on a randomly drawn card. Then the support is $S=\\{4,10\\}.$\n\nIn the stack there are $2$ cards labeled with four and $6$ cards labeled with ten (eight cards in total), so the probabilities are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(4) & =\\frac{2}{8}=\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ P(10) & =\\frac{6}{8}=\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =4\\cdot f(4)+10\\cdot f(10) \\\\  & =4(\\frac{1}{4})+10(\\frac{3}{4}) \\\\  & =1+\\frac{15}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-ceddea1b-a5cb-5c22-91ab-6571fb7ef388" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-e295c467-cba5-5269-8303-2482a80e3bd4" :answer-field/id #uuid "e295c467-cba5-5269-8303-2482a80e3bd4"] ["answer-f48698d2-8399-5591-8858-d21e6e33a4a6" :answer/id #uuid "f48698d2-8399-5591-8858-d21e6e33a4a6"] ["answer-f48698d2-8399-5591-8858-d21e6e33a4a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f48698d2-8399-5591-8858-d21e6e33a4a6" :answer/value "\\frac{17}{2}"] ["answer-field-e295c467-cba5-5269-8303-2482a80e3bd4" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-e295c467-cba5-5269-8303-2482a80e3bd4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-e295c467-cba5-5269-8303-2482a80e3bd4" :answer-field/correct "answer-f48698d2-8399-5591-8858-d21e6e33a4a6"] ["answer-field-e295c467-cba5-5269-8303-2482a80e3bd4" :answer-field/choices "answer-f48698d2-8399-5591-8858-d21e6e33a4a6"] ["question-ceddea1b-a5cb-5c22-91ab-6571fb7ef388" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-e295c467-cba5-5269-8303-2482a80e3bd4"] [17592186083309 :knowledge-point/questions "question-ceddea1b-a5cb-5c22-91ab-6571fb7ef388"] ["question-700fffbb-cd63-5378-9077-32b4c2add6e6" :question/id #uuid "700fffbb-cd63-5378-9077-32b4c2add6e6"] ["question-700fffbb-cd63-5378-9077-32b4c2add6e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-84067"] ["question-700fffbb-cd63-5378-9077-32b4c2add6e6" :question/problem "Several children were asked how many siblings they have. The number of siblings of each child was recorded below. If $X$ is the number of siblings of a randomly selected child, what is the expected value of $X?$\n\n| Number of siblings | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Number of Children | $1$ | $5$ | $3$ | $1$ |"] ["question-700fffbb-cd63-5378-9077-32b4c2add6e6" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nWe're given the frequencies of the number of siblings, so we can start by computing the corresponding probabilities. The total number of children is $1+5+3+1=10,$ so the corresponding probabilities are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=0)=f(0) & =\\frac{1}{10} \\\\ P(X=1)=f(1) & =\\frac{5}{10}=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ P(X=2)=f(2) & =\\frac{3}{10} \\\\ P(X=3)=f(3) & =\\frac{1}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe organize these results in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{3}{10}$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ |\n\nNow, summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{1}{10})+1(\\frac{1}{2})+2(\\frac{3}{10})+3(\\frac{1}{10}) \\\\  & =0+\\frac{5}{10}+\\frac{6}{10}+\\frac{3}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{0+5+6+3}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{10} \\\\  & =1.4\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-700fffbb-cd63-5378-9077-32b4c2add6e6" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-dd980177-3d4f-5c6d-a6cb-2c5b9aaa3857" :answer-field/id #uuid "dd980177-3d4f-5c6d-a6cb-2c5b9aaa3857"] ["answer-a90215ce-141d-5583-8efd-be89ae2f0bed" :answer/id #uuid "a90215ce-141d-5583-8efd-be89ae2f0bed"] ["answer-a90215ce-141d-5583-8efd-be89ae2f0bed" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a90215ce-141d-5583-8efd-be89ae2f0bed" :answer/value "0.8"] ["answer-ede15bcc-7345-509e-8ca3-6f297ed035d7" :answer/id #uuid "ede15bcc-7345-509e-8ca3-6f297ed035d7"] ["answer-ede15bcc-7345-509e-8ca3-6f297ed035d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ede15bcc-7345-509e-8ca3-6f297ed035d7" :answer/value "1"] ["answer-5c751fdf-2bec-56e1-938d-e60711842729" :answer/id #uuid "5c751fdf-2bec-56e1-938d-e60711842729"] ["answer-5c751fdf-2bec-56e1-938d-e60711842729" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-5c751fdf-2bec-56e1-938d-e60711842729" :answer/value "1.4"] ["answer-6e02a023-2534-54ea-a95d-0e9b379d35c3" :answer/id #uuid "6e02a023-2534-54ea-a95d-0e9b379d35c3"] ["answer-6e02a023-2534-54ea-a95d-0e9b379d35c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-6e02a023-2534-54ea-a95d-0e9b379d35c3" :answer/value "1.6"] ["answer-0ce3784e-cee7-5852-894c-71ed7ce007ce" :answer/id #uuid "0ce3784e-cee7-5852-894c-71ed7ce007ce"] ["answer-0ce3784e-cee7-5852-894c-71ed7ce007ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0ce3784e-cee7-5852-894c-71ed7ce007ce" :answer/value "2"] ["answer-field-dd980177-3d4f-5c6d-a6cb-2c5b9aaa3857" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-dd980177-3d4f-5c6d-a6cb-2c5b9aaa3857" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-dd980177-3d4f-5c6d-a6cb-2c5b9aaa3857" :answer-field/correct "answer-5c751fdf-2bec-56e1-938d-e60711842729"] ["answer-field-dd980177-3d4f-5c6d-a6cb-2c5b9aaa3857" :answer-field/choices "answer-a90215ce-141d-5583-8efd-be89ae2f0bed"] ["answer-field-dd980177-3d4f-5c6d-a6cb-2c5b9aaa3857" :answer-field/choices "answer-ede15bcc-7345-509e-8ca3-6f297ed035d7"] ["answer-field-dd980177-3d4f-5c6d-a6cb-2c5b9aaa3857" :answer-field/choices "answer-5c751fdf-2bec-56e1-938d-e60711842729"] ["answer-field-dd980177-3d4f-5c6d-a6cb-2c5b9aaa3857" :answer-field/choices "answer-6e02a023-2534-54ea-a95d-0e9b379d35c3"] ["answer-field-dd980177-3d4f-5c6d-a6cb-2c5b9aaa3857" :answer-field/choices "answer-0ce3784e-cee7-5852-894c-71ed7ce007ce"] ["question-700fffbb-cd63-5378-9077-32b4c2add6e6" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-dd980177-3d4f-5c6d-a6cb-2c5b9aaa3857"] [17592186083309 :knowledge-point/questions "question-700fffbb-cd63-5378-9077-32b4c2add6e6"] ["question-41c4d9f2-fb24-5742-893b-e72bc5478b30" :question/id #uuid "41c4d9f2-fb24-5742-893b-e72bc5478b30"] ["question-41c4d9f2-fb24-5742-893b-e72bc5478b30" :question/math-academy-id "q-276300"] ["question-41c4d9f2-fb24-5742-893b-e72bc5478b30" :question/problem "A quality control manager at a warehouse inspects electronic boxes for defective items. The number of faulty items in each box was recorded and summarized below. If $X$ is the number of faulty items in a box, what is the expected value of $X?$\n\n| Number of Boxes | $13$ | $6$ | $4$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Faulty Items | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n\n$\\text{E}[X]=$\n{{field-1}}"] ["question-41c4d9f2-fb24-5742-893b-e72bc5478b30" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nWe're given the frequencies of the faulty items, so we can start by computing the corresponding probabilities. The total number of boxes is $13+6+4+2=25,$ so the corresponding probabilities are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=0)=f(0) & =\\frac{13}{25} \\\\ P(X=1)=f(1) & =\\frac{6}{25} \\\\ P(X=2)=f(2) & =\\frac{4}{25} \\\\ P(X=3)=f(3) & =\\frac{2}{25}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe organize these results in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{13}{25}$ | $\\frac{6}{25}$ | $\\frac{4}{25}$ | $\\frac{2}{25}$ |\n\nNow, summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{13}{25})+1(\\frac{6}{25})+2(\\frac{4}{25})+3(\\frac{2}{25}) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{25}+\\frac{8}{25}+\\frac{6}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{6+8+6}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-41c4d9f2-fb24-5742-893b-e72bc5478b30" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-55e2ebfb-2990-504c-a3b7-16d650b15125" :answer-field/id #uuid "55e2ebfb-2990-504c-a3b7-16d650b15125"] ["answer-a3a5e633-756d-5e3a-8fa9-0ed6225a69ee" :answer/id #uuid "a3a5e633-756d-5e3a-8fa9-0ed6225a69ee"] ["answer-a3a5e633-756d-5e3a-8fa9-0ed6225a69ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a3a5e633-756d-5e3a-8fa9-0ed6225a69ee" :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}"] ["answer-field-55e2ebfb-2990-504c-a3b7-16d650b15125" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-55e2ebfb-2990-504c-a3b7-16d650b15125" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-55e2ebfb-2990-504c-a3b7-16d650b15125" :answer-field/correct "answer-a3a5e633-756d-5e3a-8fa9-0ed6225a69ee"] ["answer-field-55e2ebfb-2990-504c-a3b7-16d650b15125" :answer-field/choices "answer-a3a5e633-756d-5e3a-8fa9-0ed6225a69ee"] ["question-41c4d9f2-fb24-5742-893b-e72bc5478b30" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-55e2ebfb-2990-504c-a3b7-16d650b15125"] [17592186083309 :knowledge-point/questions "question-41c4d9f2-fb24-5742-893b-e72bc5478b30"] ["question-d599b4ec-9437-5cdd-aa0b-91b4481a6586" :question/id #uuid "d599b4ec-9437-5cdd-aa0b-91b4481a6586"] ["question-d599b4ec-9437-5cdd-aa0b-91b4481a6586" :question/math-academy-id "q-89157"] ["question-d599b4ec-9437-5cdd-aa0b-91b4481a6586" :question/problem "Several households were asked the number of children that lived there. The number of children in each was recorded below. If $X$ is the number of children that live at a randomly selected household, what is the expected value of $X?$\n\n| Number of Children | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Number of Households | $6$ | $9$ | $6$ | $3$ |"] ["question-d599b4ec-9437-5cdd-aa0b-91b4481a6586" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nWe're given the frequencies of the number of childen, so we can start by computing the corresponding probabilities. The total number of households is $3+9+6+6=24,$ so the corresponding probabilities are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=1)=f(1) & =\\frac{6}{24}=\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ P(X=2)=f(2) & =\\frac{9}{24}=\\frac{3}{8} \\\\ P(X=3)=f(3) & =\\frac{6}{24}=\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ P(X=4)=f(4) & =\\frac{3}{24}=\\frac{1}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe organize these results in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n\nNow, summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{4})+2(\\frac{3}{8})+3(\\frac{1}{4})+4(\\frac{1}{8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{2}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+3+3+2}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4} \\\\  & =2.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-d599b4ec-9437-5cdd-aa0b-91b4481a6586" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-618772c4-492e-57e3-9e76-dc9f3ada338c" :answer-field/id #uuid "618772c4-492e-57e3-9e76-dc9f3ada338c"] ["answer-c5540b63-e212-55cb-b7a9-7c7a2846f551" :answer/id #uuid "c5540b63-e212-55cb-b7a9-7c7a2846f551"] ["answer-c5540b63-e212-55cb-b7a9-7c7a2846f551" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c5540b63-e212-55cb-b7a9-7c7a2846f551" :answer/value "1.5"] ["answer-7566e7ed-5b8d-55f6-bcd8-3e0711ba276d" :answer/id #uuid "7566e7ed-5b8d-55f6-bcd8-3e0711ba276d"] ["answer-7566e7ed-5b8d-55f6-bcd8-3e0711ba276d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-7566e7ed-5b8d-55f6-bcd8-3e0711ba276d" :answer/value "1.75"] ["answer-c95ceba2-efcb-54f1-bc4a-d6b2a95fef1a" :answer/id #uuid "c95ceba2-efcb-54f1-bc4a-d6b2a95fef1a"] ["answer-c95ceba2-efcb-54f1-bc4a-d6b2a95fef1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c95ceba2-efcb-54f1-bc4a-d6b2a95fef1a" :answer/value "2"] ["answer-2a02737d-84cc-5b65-a38a-d8f95f1427b0" :answer/id #uuid "2a02737d-84cc-5b65-a38a-d8f95f1427b0"] ["answer-2a02737d-84cc-5b65-a38a-d8f95f1427b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-2a02737d-84cc-5b65-a38a-d8f95f1427b0" :answer/value "2.25"] ["answer-93cd1bc1-ffd4-50f6-955c-6bee087d74b2" :answer/id #uuid "93cd1bc1-ffd4-50f6-955c-6bee087d74b2"] ["answer-93cd1bc1-ffd4-50f6-955c-6bee087d74b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-93cd1bc1-ffd4-50f6-955c-6bee087d74b2" :answer/value "2.5"] ["answer-field-618772c4-492e-57e3-9e76-dc9f3ada338c" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-618772c4-492e-57e3-9e76-dc9f3ada338c" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-618772c4-492e-57e3-9e76-dc9f3ada338c" :answer-field/correct "answer-2a02737d-84cc-5b65-a38a-d8f95f1427b0"] ["answer-field-618772c4-492e-57e3-9e76-dc9f3ada338c" :answer-field/choices "answer-c5540b63-e212-55cb-b7a9-7c7a2846f551"] ["answer-field-618772c4-492e-57e3-9e76-dc9f3ada338c" :answer-field/choices "answer-7566e7ed-5b8d-55f6-bcd8-3e0711ba276d"] ["answer-field-618772c4-492e-57e3-9e76-dc9f3ada338c" :answer-field/choices "answer-c95ceba2-efcb-54f1-bc4a-d6b2a95fef1a"] ["answer-field-618772c4-492e-57e3-9e76-dc9f3ada338c" :answer-field/choices "answer-2a02737d-84cc-5b65-a38a-d8f95f1427b0"] ["answer-field-618772c4-492e-57e3-9e76-dc9f3ada338c" :answer-field/choices "answer-93cd1bc1-ffd4-50f6-955c-6bee087d74b2"] ["question-d599b4ec-9437-5cdd-aa0b-91b4481a6586" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-618772c4-492e-57e3-9e76-dc9f3ada338c"] [17592186083309 :knowledge-point/questions "question-d599b4ec-9437-5cdd-aa0b-91b4481a6586"] ["question-068e9bc7-6f46-5ac9-a057-d5f4aa9a8aeb" :question/id #uuid "068e9bc7-6f46-5ac9-a057-d5f4aa9a8aeb"] ["question-068e9bc7-6f46-5ac9-a057-d5f4aa9a8aeb" :question/math-academy-id "q-127818"] ["question-068e9bc7-6f46-5ac9-a057-d5f4aa9a8aeb" :question/problem "One way to bet in roulette is to place $\\$1$ on a single number. If the ball lands on that number, the player wins $\\$35.$ If the ball lands on any of the other $37$ slots, the player doesn't win. What is the expected profit, rounded to the nearest dollar, for a player who plays one hundred games on number $12$ in a row?"] ["question-068e9bc7-6f46-5ac9-a057-d5f4aa9a8aeb" :question/worked-solution "First of all, profit is revenue minus cost, or in our case, winnings minus cost. So, once we have found the expected winnings after one hundred games, we need to subtract $100\\cdot 1=100$ dollars to account for the price of playing.\n\nNow, let's find the expected winnings and summarize them in a table. If $W$ is the winnings (in dollars) on a single game, and $f(w)$ is the probability mass function for $W,$ then we have the following:\n\n| $f(w)$ | $\\frac{1}{38}$ | $\\frac{37}{38}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $w$ | $35$ | $0$ |\n\nThe expected value of $W$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[W] & =35\\cdot f(35)+0\\cdot f(0) \\\\  & =35(\\frac{1}{38})+0(\\frac{37}{38}) \\\\  & =\\frac{35}{38} \\\\  & ≈0.92.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis represents the expected winnings for a single game. So, the expected winnings for $100$ games  on number $12$ is\n\n$$\n100\\cdot \\text{E}[W]=100\\cdot (0.92)=92.\n$$\n\nNow, subtracting the $100$ dollars paid to play, we get that the expected profit (in dollars) is\n\n$$\nE[p]=92-100=-8.\n$$"] ["question-068e9bc7-6f46-5ac9-a057-d5f4aa9a8aeb" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-53865da6-8e44-5bb9-8d40-4d2805caf8a7" :answer-field/id #uuid "53865da6-8e44-5bb9-8d40-4d2805caf8a7"] ["answer-1bec36d6-dfb7-5749-9664-f7f73dc25b79" :answer/id #uuid "1bec36d6-dfb7-5749-9664-f7f73dc25b79"] ["answer-1bec36d6-dfb7-5749-9664-f7f73dc25b79" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-1bec36d6-dfb7-5749-9664-f7f73dc25b79" :answer/value "$-\\$10$"] ["answer-2e9bbeaf-98e6-558c-81d6-d0813fc9f4ac" :answer/id #uuid "2e9bbeaf-98e6-558c-81d6-d0813fc9f4ac"] ["answer-2e9bbeaf-98e6-558c-81d6-d0813fc9f4ac" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-2e9bbeaf-98e6-558c-81d6-d0813fc9f4ac" :answer/value "$-\\$19$"] ["answer-b1e0eb6a-bd70-5f35-a14d-f4f095208cc4" :answer/id #uuid "b1e0eb6a-bd70-5f35-a14d-f4f095208cc4"] ["answer-b1e0eb6a-bd70-5f35-a14d-f4f095208cc4" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-b1e0eb6a-bd70-5f35-a14d-f4f095208cc4" :answer/value "$-\\$8$"] ["answer-59a5f4bc-a0cc-5d8a-b1c9-87ca178ebcf7" :answer/id #uuid "59a5f4bc-a0cc-5d8a-b1c9-87ca178ebcf7"] ["answer-59a5f4bc-a0cc-5d8a-b1c9-87ca178ebcf7" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-59a5f4bc-a0cc-5d8a-b1c9-87ca178ebcf7" :answer/value "$\\$7$"] ["answer-8e4ee2a5-d371-5586-98ed-838864441766" :answer/id #uuid "8e4ee2a5-d371-5586-98ed-838864441766"] ["answer-8e4ee2a5-d371-5586-98ed-838864441766" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-8e4ee2a5-d371-5586-98ed-838864441766" :answer/value "$\\$9$"] ["answer-field-53865da6-8e44-5bb9-8d40-4d2805caf8a7" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-53865da6-8e44-5bb9-8d40-4d2805caf8a7" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-53865da6-8e44-5bb9-8d40-4d2805caf8a7" :answer-field/correct "answer-b1e0eb6a-bd70-5f35-a14d-f4f095208cc4"] ["answer-field-53865da6-8e44-5bb9-8d40-4d2805caf8a7" :answer-field/choices "answer-1bec36d6-dfb7-5749-9664-f7f73dc25b79"] ["answer-field-53865da6-8e44-5bb9-8d40-4d2805caf8a7" :answer-field/choices "answer-2e9bbeaf-98e6-558c-81d6-d0813fc9f4ac"] ["answer-field-53865da6-8e44-5bb9-8d40-4d2805caf8a7" :answer-field/choices "answer-b1e0eb6a-bd70-5f35-a14d-f4f095208cc4"] ["answer-field-53865da6-8e44-5bb9-8d40-4d2805caf8a7" :answer-field/choices "answer-59a5f4bc-a0cc-5d8a-b1c9-87ca178ebcf7"] ["answer-field-53865da6-8e44-5bb9-8d40-4d2805caf8a7" :answer-field/choices "answer-8e4ee2a5-d371-5586-98ed-838864441766"] ["question-068e9bc7-6f46-5ac9-a057-d5f4aa9a8aeb" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-53865da6-8e44-5bb9-8d40-4d2805caf8a7"] [17592186083273 :knowledge-point/questions "question-068e9bc7-6f46-5ac9-a057-d5f4aa9a8aeb"] ["question-267e0e90-b604-5e86-ad43-795951237ad2" :question/id #uuid "267e0e90-b604-5e86-ad43-795951237ad2"] ["question-267e0e90-b604-5e86-ad43-795951237ad2" :question/math-academy-id "q-337346"] ["question-267e0e90-b604-5e86-ad43-795951237ad2" :question/problem "One way to bet in roulette is to place $\\$2$ on a single number. If the ball lands on that number, the player wins $\\$70.$ If the ball lands on any of the other $37$ slots, the player doesn't win. What is the expected profit, rounded to the nearest dollar, for a player who plays one hundred games on number $8$ in a row?\n\nThe expected profit in dollars is $E(p)=$\n{{field-1}}"] ["question-267e0e90-b604-5e86-ad43-795951237ad2" :question/worked-solution "First of all, profit is revenue minus cost, or in our case, winnings minus cost. So, once we have found the expected winnings after one hundred games, we need to subtract $100\\cdot 2=200$ dollars to account for the price of playing.\n\nNow, let's find the expected winnings and summarize them in a table. If $W$ is the winnings (in dollars) on a single game, and $f(w)$ is the probability mass function for $W,$ then we have the following:\n\n| $f(w)$ | $\\frac{1}{38}$ | $\\frac{37}{38}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $w$ | $70$ | $0$ |\n\nThe expected value of $W$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[W] & =70\\cdot f(70)+0\\cdot f(0) \\\\  & =70(\\frac{1}{38})+0(\\frac{37}{38}) \\\\  & =\\frac{70}{38} \\\\  & ≈1.84.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis represents the expected winnings for a single game. So, the expected winnings for $100$ games on number $8$ is\n\n$$\n100\\cdot \\text{E}[W]=100\\cdot (1.84)=184.\n$$\n\nNow, subtracting the $200$ dollars paid to play, we get that the expected profit (in dollars) is\n\n$$\nE[p]=184-200=-16.\n$$"] ["question-267e0e90-b604-5e86-ad43-795951237ad2" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-4197adf1-104f-52af-a2fe-ce58ae6658aa" :answer-field/id #uuid "4197adf1-104f-52af-a2fe-ce58ae6658aa"] ["answer-f39199e8-353c-5632-85b5-146e5d346bc2" :answer/id #uuid "f39199e8-353c-5632-85b5-146e5d346bc2"] ["answer-f39199e8-353c-5632-85b5-146e5d346bc2" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f39199e8-353c-5632-85b5-146e5d346bc2" :answer/value "-16"] ["answer-field-4197adf1-104f-52af-a2fe-ce58ae6658aa" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-4197adf1-104f-52af-a2fe-ce58ae6658aa" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-4197adf1-104f-52af-a2fe-ce58ae6658aa" :answer-field/correct "answer-f39199e8-353c-5632-85b5-146e5d346bc2"] ["answer-field-4197adf1-104f-52af-a2fe-ce58ae6658aa" :answer-field/choices "answer-f39199e8-353c-5632-85b5-146e5d346bc2"] ["question-267e0e90-b604-5e86-ad43-795951237ad2" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-4197adf1-104f-52af-a2fe-ce58ae6658aa"] [17592186083273 :knowledge-point/questions "question-267e0e90-b604-5e86-ad43-795951237ad2"] [17592186083425 :activity/expected-seconds 960.0]] "retractions" [[17592186357384 :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the spin of the fair spinner. Then the support is $S={-2,-1,1,3,5,6},$ and the corresponding probabilities are all $\\frac{1}{6}:$\n\n$$\nf(-2)=f(-1)=f(1)=f(3)=f(5)=f(6)=\\frac{1}{6}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =(-2)\\cdot f(-2)+(-1)\\cdot f(-1)+1\\cdot f(1)+3\\cdot f(3)+5\\cdot f(5)+6\\cdot f(6) \\\\  & =(-2)(\\frac{1}{6})+(-1)(\\frac{1}{6})+1(\\frac{1}{6})+3(\\frac{1}{6})+5(\\frac{1}{6})+6(\\frac{1}{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{-2}{6}+\\frac{-1}{6}+\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{3}{6}+\\frac{5}{6}+\\frac{6}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2-1+1+3+5+6}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{6} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186370946 :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the value of a randomly drawn bill. Then the support is $S={5,10,20}.$\n\nIn the bag there are  $4$ five-dollar bills, $8$ ten-dollar bills and $6$ twenty-dollar bills (eighteen bills in total), so the probabilities are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(5) & =\\frac{4}{18}=\\frac{2}{9} \\\\ P(10) & =\\frac{8}{18}=\\frac{4}{9} \\\\ P(20) & =\\frac{6}{18}=\\frac{3}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =5\\cdot f(5)+10\\cdot f(10)+20\\cdot f(20) \\\\  & =5(\\frac{2}{9})+10(\\frac{4}{9})+20(\\frac{3}{9}) \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{9}+\\frac{40}{9}+\\frac{60}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{10+40+60}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{110}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"]]}]